What is Prometheus?
      Prometheus is an open-source monitoring and alerting system that collects, stores, and queries metrics from applications, servers, and Kubernetes clusters.
Think of Prometheus as a database specialized for time-based metrics.

ex:
| Time  | CPU % | Memory % | Requests/sec |
| ----- | ----- | -------- | ------------ |
| 10:00 | 25    | 40       | 120          |
| 10:01 | 30    | 41       | 130          |
| 10:02 | 45    | 43       | 150          |

Unlike a traditional database that stores business data (users, orders, products), Prometheus stores metrics over time.



Why do we need Prometheus?
      Imagine your application suddenly becomes slow.

Without Prometheus, you might only know:
      "The application is slow."

You don't know:

CPU usage
Memory usage
Disk usage
Network traffic
Number of requests
Error rate
JVM heap usage
Which pod is unhealthy

Prometheus collects all this information continuously.



What is a Metric?
        A metric is a numerical measurement of something.

Examples:

CPU usage: CPU = 45%
Memory usage:Memory = 2.4 GB
HTTP requests: 150 requests/sec
Disk usage: 80%
JVM Threads: 42 Threads

Everything Prometheus stores is a metric.



