Prometheus pulls metrics from exporters and applications at regular intervals.


Main Components:
1. Prometheus Server
    This is the heart of the system.

Responsibilities:

Scrapes metrics
Stores metrics
Executes queries
Evaluates alert rules
Sends alerts to Alertmanager

Think of it as the brain.



2. Exporters
    Prometheus doesn't magically know CPU or memory usage.

It needs exporters.

Example:

Linux Server

CPU

↓

Node Exporter

↓

Prometheus

Common exporters:

| Exporter          | Purpose                |
| ----------------- | ---------------------- |
| Node Exporter     | Linux metrics          |
| Blackbox Exporter | HTTP, TCP, ICMP checks |
| MySQL Exporter    | MySQL metrics          |
| Redis Exporter    | Redis metrics          |
| JMX Exporter      | Java/JVM metrics       |
| NGINX Exporter    | NGINX metrics          |

3. Targets
    A target is anything Prometheus scrapes.

Examples:

10.0.0.5:9100
10.0.0.20:8080/metrics
pod-abc:8080

Each target exposes metrics.



Pull Model:

Prometheus uses a pull model.

Every 15 seconds

Prometheus

↓

GET /metrics

↓

Application

↓

Returns Metrics

↓

Prometheus Stores Them

Unlike some monitoring systems that push metrics, Prometheus regularly requests them.



Metrics Endpoint: Applications expose a /metrics endpoint.

Example:
http://app:8080/metrics

Example response:
http_requests_total 150

cpu_usage 45

memory_usage_bytes 2147483648

jvm_threads_current 28

Prometheus reads this text and stores it.



